<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We restate the theorem for convenience.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Information Ceiling)<span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{in}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a zero-mean random vector with finite
covariance <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\!x}\!=\!\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\!\top}]\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝐱𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\!x}\!=\!\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{x}\mathbf{x}^{\!\top}]\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let the down-projection and the deterministic post-mapping be</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=A\mathbf{x},\quad\mathbf{v}=B\mathbf{u},\,A\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{r\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},\;B\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times r}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=A\mathbf{x},\quad\mathbf{v}=B\mathbf{u},\,A\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{r\times d_{\mathrm{in}}},\;B\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{out}}\times r}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{v})\;\leq\;\frac{1}{2}\log\!\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+A\Sigma_{\!x}A^{\!\top}\bigr),\,r(\mathbf{u})\leq r(A)\leq r.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:1.313em;" width="1.313em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.177em;" width="1.177em"><mo movablelimits="false">det</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{v})\;\leq\;\frac{1}{2}\log\!\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+A\Sigma_{\!x}A^{\!\top}\bigr),\,r(\mathbf{u})\leq r(A)\leq r.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (Data-processing).<span id="A2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Because <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}=B\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}=B\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic
function of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the chain
<math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbf{u}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbf{u}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math>
is Markov; the data-processing inequality (DPI) gives:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{v})\;\leq\;I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{u})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{v})\;\leq\;I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{u}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Gaussian upper envelope).<span id="A2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Denote by <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}}\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma_{\!x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}}\!\sim\!\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma_{\!x})</annotation></semantics></math> a <em id="A2.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gaussian</em> vector sharing the same second-order moment as <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}}\!=\!A\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}}\!=\!A\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The joint pair <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}},\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}},\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}})</annotation></semantics></math> has the same mean, covariance and cross-covariance as <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{u})</annotation></semantics></math> because both involve the <em id="A2.p3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> linear map <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Under these matched second-order constraints, the Gaussian pair maximises mutual information, hence</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{u})\;\leq\;I(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}};\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\mathbf{x};\mathbf{u})\;\leq\;I(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}};\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Closed form for linear–Gaussian).<span id="A2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
For jointly Gaussian variables linked by a deterministic linear map,
<math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,I(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}};\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}})\!=\!\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+A\Sigma_{\!x}A^{\!\top}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.177em;" width="1.177em"><mo>det</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,I(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{G}};\mathbf{u}_{\mathrm{G}})\!=\!\tfrac{1}{2}\log\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+A\Sigma_{\!x}A^{\!\top}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4 (Chain the bounds).<span id="A2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Combining
(<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ MASA: Rethinking the Representational Bottleneck in LoRA with Multi-A Shared Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)–(<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ MASA: Rethinking the Representational Bottleneck in LoRA with Multi-A Shared Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) with Step 3 yields the desired mutual-information bound
(<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Theorem 2 (Information Ceiling). ‣ Appendix B Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ MASA: Rethinking the Representational Bottleneck in LoRA with Multi-A Shared Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The rank inequality follows from the
sub-multiplicativity of rank:
<math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\mathbf{u})=r(A\mathbf{x})\leq r(A)\leq r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\mathbf{u})=r(A\mathbf{x})\leq r(A)\leq r</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Tightness.</em>
Equality in (<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Theorem 2 (Information Ceiling). ‣ Appendix B Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ MASA: Rethinking the Representational Bottleneck in LoRA with Multi-A Shared Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) is attained when <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{u})</annotation></semantics></math> is itself jointly Gaussian, <em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">irrespective of</em> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Why multi-<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> lifts the ceiling.</em>
Replacing <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> by an ensemble <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and
aggregating <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{u}}=\sum_{i}A_{i}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{u}}=\sum_{i}A_{i}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> preserves the rank constraint, but
increases
<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+\!\sum_{i}A_{i}\Sigma_{\!x}A_{i}^{\!\top}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.177em;" width="1.177em"><mo>det</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.026em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.026em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\!\bigl(I_{r}+\!\sum_{i}A_{i}\Sigma_{\!x}A_{i}^{\!\top}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>
whenever the row-spaces of the <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are not perfectly aligned, thereby
raising the right-hand side of (<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Theorem 2 (Information Ceiling). ‣ Appendix B Appendix A Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ MASA: Rethinking the Representational Bottleneck in LoRA with Multi-A Shared Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
